**Incident Report Summary:**

The network forensic analysis confirms a NetSupport RAT infection on enterprise workstation DESKTOP-B8TQK49 logged in by user oboomwald. Suricata/ET Pro signatures provided definitive malware identification. The attack chain shows SMB-based exploitation (detected at 08:49:55 UTC) followed by RAT initialization and C2 beaconing (started 08:50:45 UTC to 194.180.191.64:443). The malware executed HTTP POST checks to a hardcoded C2 endpoint every few seconds. Auxiliary suspicious activity includes DNS lookups and TLS connections to modandcrackedapk.com, a flagged ZPHP malware domain, indicating possible secondary payload delivery infrastructure.
